Title: gaze close refuses a review worktree holding a regenerable egg-info build artifact
Created: 2026-10-29
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-29T19:08Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
Reported by the DOIfetch session (raid f9e483, 2026-10-29) through the inter-project
protocol. On DOIfetch PRs #15, #16 and #17 (#17 twice), gaze ran `uv run` in
`.claude/worktrees/review-<N>`, which created `.venv/`, `doifetch.egg-info/`,
`__pycache__/` and `.pytest_cache/`, all gitignored. Then `scripts/gaze_close.py` `cleanup()`
refused to remove the tree, and gaze recorded ESCALATE on notes although the review found
nothing blocking. The raid had to re-run gaze to get a usable record.
That blocks a merge. Positive control (DOIfetch): plain `git worktree remove` succeeds
with those files present.

Isolated 2026-10-29 (lair session): `worktree_residue` in `scripts/worktree-clean-lib.sh`
treats ignored paths as residue except `.tmp/`, root `.venv/` and tool caches
(`__pycache__`, `.pytest_cache`, `.ruff_cache`, `.mypy_cache`). The function feeds
`worktree-exit-preflight.sh --removal`, which `gaze_close.py` calls.
Repro in a scratch repo with the four paths: the residue printed only `!! doifetch.egg-info/`;
with the egg-info removed it printed nothing. `*.egg-info/` is regenerated by any
`uv run` or `uv sync` of a packaged project, so every gaze of a Python package with
a setuptools build backend hits it.

## Scope
- Count `*.egg-info/` (ignored, at any depth) as regenerable in `worktree_residue`.
- Check for other build outputs that `uv run` regenerates (for example `build/` from
  setuptools). Add only the ones that are regenerated and never hand-made, and keep
  `build/panel-head` handled by gaze_close as it is today.
- The library is shared with `worktree-gc.sh`, so check that the same widening holds there.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A test fails on the current code: a tree whose only ignored entries are `.venv/`, `x.egg-info/`, `__pycache__/` and `.pytest_cache/` reports residue
- [ ] With the fix, that tree reports no residue, and an ignored hand-made file (for example `notes.txt` under an ignored `*`) still does
- [ ] `gaze_close.py` cleanup removes such a review tree (test or one real gaze on a DOIfetch PR)
